+ .TP
++.B -N, --netdev-cpus=<interface-pattern:cpulist>
++Restrict IRQs of matching PCI network interfaces to the specified CPU list,
++while continuing automatic load balancing within that pool. Interface patterns
++use shell wildcard syntax and should be quoted. The option is repeatable;
++all matching rules (including interfaces sharing an IRQ) are intersected.
++Online CPUs and global CPU bans further restrict the pool. Nonmatching IRQs
++retain their normal policy. For example:
++.B --netdev-cpus='enp*:0-3,8-11'
++No IRQ numbers or CPU pools are built in. An empty effective pool is reported;
++irqbalance leaves the current affinity unchanged rather than violating the
++pool. Explicitly banned or unmanaged IRQs remain unmanaged. New PCI IRQs and
++CPU hotplug use the rules; request SIGHUP after an interface rename or if
++the netdev appears after its IRQ was initially discovered.
++.TP
